<observation>I'll search for DIA-NN command line arguments and parameters documentation.Based on the search results, I can provide you with information about DIA-NN command line arguments and parameters. Here's the documentation:

## DIA-NN Command Line Overview

DIA-NN provides a graphical user interface (GUI) that invokes an underlying command-line tool (diann.exe, diann-linux or a container). The command-line tool can also be used separately, e.g. as part of custom automated processing pipelines.(Citation: GitHub - vdemichev/DiaNN: DIA-NN - a universal automated software suite for DIA proteomics data analysis. · GitHub - https://github.com/vdemichev/DiaNN)

## Command Line Syntax

All these options start with a double dash -- followed by the option name and, if applicable, some parameters to be set. Any option prefixed with -- in this guide should be entered in the Additional options text field.(Citation: GitHub - vdemichev/DiaNN: DIA-NN - a universal automated software suite for DIA proteomics data analysis. · GitHub - https://github.com/vdemichev/DiaNN)

## Common Command Line Arguments

Based on the search results, here are key command line parameters:

### Input/Output Options:
- `--fasta` - Specify FASTA file(s) for protein annotation or in silico digest
- `--cfg` - Use a configuration file
- `--out` - Specify output report file (e.g., report.tsv)
- `--dir` - Specify output directory
- `--f` - Input raw data files

### Processing Options:
- `--threads` - Number of CPU threads to use
- `--fasta-search` - Perform library-free search with FASTA digest
- `--predictor` - Generate spectral library using deep learning
- `--fasta-filter` - Filter peptides using a command like "--fasta-filter C:/human_peptides.fasta"(Citation: DIA-NN GUI Manual - https://usermanual.wiki/Document/DIANN20GUI20manual.1528310561/help)

### Analysis Options:
- `--relaxed-prot-inf` - Recommended for benchmarking when inferring proteins to estimate identifiable protein groups per run(Citation: Github vdemichev/diann Source - https://www.faqgit.com/repositories/vdemichev/DiaNN?id=113714)
- `--no-stats` - Turn off generation of statistics file(Citation: DIA-NN GUI Manual - https://usermanual.wiki/Document/DIANN20GUI20manual.1528310561/help)
- `--pipeline` - Run a pipeline from the command line(Citation: GitHub - vdemichev/DiaNN: DIA-NN - a universal automated software suite for DIA proteomics data analysis. · GitHub - https://github.com/vdemichev/DiaNN)

## Example Usage

A basic command structure: diann --threads $SLURM_CPUS_PER_TASK --fasta /data/$USER/project/input.fasta --cfg /data/$USER/project/config_file --out report.tsv --dir /data/$USER/project/output_dir(Citation: diann - https://hpc.nih.gov/apps/diann.html)

## Finding Complete Reference

The full reference is provided in Command-line reference(Citation: GitHub - vdemichev/DiaNN: DIA-NN - a universal automated software suite for DIA proteomics data analysis. · GitHub - https://github.com/vdemichev/DiaNN) section of the DIA-NN documentation on GitHub. When the GUI launches the command-line tool, it prints in the Log panel the exact set of commands it used(Citation: GitHub - vdemichev/DiaNN: DIA-NN - a universal automated software suite for DIA proteomics data analysis. · GitHub - https://github.com/vdemichev/DiaNN), which can help you understand the command line syntax.

For the most comprehensive and up-to-date command-line reference, I recommend visiting the official DIA-NN GitHub repository at https://github.com/vdemichev/DiaNN where the full documentation is maintained.
</observation>
